**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
sim_build/
.claude-assets/
.private/
.claude-recent-session-id

# Simulation artefacts
results.xml

# Yosys/Nextpnr byproducts + huge synth artefacts
abc.history
synth/lattice/reports/*.json
synth/lattice/reports/*.log
synth/lattice/reports/*.rpt
synth/lattice/reports/*.config
synth/lattice/reports/*.bit

# Vivado byproducts + huge checkpoints (2026-08-13)
# .dcp are 129 MB of binary; regenerate with `make synth-pod/impl-pod PART=...`
# (see .claude-memos/cross_vendor_fabric_evidence.md §6)
synth/checkpoints/*.dcp
# Router congestion dumps — kept locally as evidence, too bulky/noisy to track
cong/
iter_*_CongestedCLBsAndNets.txt
# GATE S1 ECP5 half (spec §28.7): the nextpnr input netlist for the whole
# system top is 40 MB — 5x the largest tracked fp-ops netlist (fp_stepseq
# 7.9 MB) and 15x the repo's own .dcp threshold rationale. The measurement
# EVIDENCE (_synth.rpt stat, _premap.rpt, _pnr.log) is tracked; the netlist
# is regenerated by
#   sh synth/lattice/scripts/synth_fp_ops.sh sys_top_core
synth/lattice/reports/fp_ops/sys_top_core_synth.json

# GATE S1 (spec §28) run artefacts. The *_run.log IS tracked evidence — the
# CRITICAL WARNING census is a binding gate axis and must be greppable by a
# reviewer. The journal carries no evidence, and Vivado renames the previous
# log/journal to *_<pid>.backup.* on a re-run, which would otherwise pile up
# duplicates of the tracked log.
synth/reports/fp_ops/*_run.jou
synth/reports/fp_ops/*.backup.log
synth/reports/fp_ops/*.backup.jou

# TLC model checker scratch (proofs/tla/)
proofs/tla/states/
proofs/tla/*.old
# TLC 는 불변식 위반 run 마다 반례 trace 를 모듈 옆에 뱉는다.
# run.sh 는 MUST-FAIL 을 14건 의도적으로 돌리므로 **게이트를 한 번
# 돌릴 때마다 트리가 더러워진다** (실측: 1회 실행에 42개). 커밋된 적
# 없는 순수 부산물이다 — 증거는 derived/traces/ 에 별도로 보존된다.
proofs/tla/*_TTrace_*.tla
proofs/tla/*_TTrace_*.bin

# Vivado CWD scratch for `make synth-sys-gate` (keeps clockInfo.txt/.Xil out
# of the repo root — the gate reports themselves are tracked, this is not).
synth/reports/fp_ops/.sysgate_cwd/

# Vivado REPO-ROOT scratch (2026-08-18 clean-up). A Vivado run launched from
# the repo root drops its journal/log and clockInfo.txt into the cwd. These
# were tracked by accident: all 12 root vivado*.{jou,log} had exactly ONE
# commit each (the one that added them) and zero content changes since, and
# `grep -rn` finds no consumer for any of them. `make synth-sys-gate` now
# runs from .sysgate_cwd/ above, so new runs never reach the root.
#
# !! EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ROOT-ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH ON PURPOSE. !!
# `synth/reports/fp_ops/*_run.log` is BINDING gate evidence (spec §28 — the
# CRITICAL WARNING census must stay greppable). An unanchored `vivado.log` or
# `*.log` would be a foot-gun the moment someone renames a report; the anchor
# makes it structurally impossible for these five lines to reach that file.
/clockInfo.txt
/vivado.jou
/vivado.log
/vivado_*.backup.jou
/vivado_*.backup.log

# Per-user Claude Code runtime (see .claude-memories/memory_backup_pattern.md
# §5 — this file was on that memo's prescribed ignore list but the rule was
# never added, so a dead PID snapshot from 2026-05-02 sat in git). NOT to be
# confused with .claude/session-end-hook.sh, which is real infrastructure and
# stays tracked.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

